For a 5 V to 3.3 V LDO delivering 2 A, the approximate pass-element
dissipation is:

P = (VIN - VOUT) × IOUT

P = (5 - 3.3) × 2 = 3.4 W

This is substantial heat for a small PCB. The actual thermal result
depends on package, copper area, airflow, and thermal resistance.
Regulator selection must be based on the load, noise needs, efficiency,
and thermal design.

