The THEJAS32 SoC is the central processing block in the intended FCNS
architecture. It is expected to communicate with peripherals and execute
the firmware that processes sensor measurements and pilot commands.

The controller's actual peripheral availability, voltage domains, boot
process, and pin assignments must be confirmed using the exact device
documentation. A net label alone does not prove that a chosen pin
