16. Conclusion

The THEJAS32-based FPV Flight Control and Navigation System schematic
brings together power management, controller circuitry, primary and
secondary motion sensors, a barometric pressure sensor, GNSS and compass
interfaces, USB/UART connectivity, external flash, receiver and ESC
connections, telemetry, video-related circuitry, and status indicators.

Together, these blocks provide a hardware foundation for a
flight-control platform. The controller is intended to acquire
measurements, process pilot commands, execute the flight-control
firmware, and generate motor-control signals for external ESCs.

The quality and reliability of the final system depend on correct
component selection, verified pin assignments, regulator and thermal
calculations, careful PCB layout, compatible firmware, and staged
hardware testing. The schematic should therefore be treated as a design
to verify---not as proof that the completed board is already
flight-ready.

